  "result": "I fixed all three problems. I haven't run the test suite or type-checked the changes.\n\n- **Switching off now sticks** (`src/server/repositories/webhook-repository.ts`): `updateEndpoint` skipped `enabled` whenever it was `false`. It now writes `enabled` whenever it's provided, so switching an endpoint off and back on both save. Once it's off, the existing check in `enqueueForOrg` stops new deliveries from being queued for it.\n- **Queued deliveries for off endpoints fail** (`src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`): when the delivery run reaches a delivery whose endpoint is switched off, it marks the delivery failed and counts it as failed. A missing endpoint was already handled that way. Deliveries for endpoints that are still on go out as before.\n- **Off endpoints count toward the plan allowance** (`src/server/services/webhook-service.ts`): `createWebhook` now counts every endpoint in the workspace, not just the enabled ones. A workspace at its plan limit is refused even after switching one off.",
